{{also|antibiòtic}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|antibiotique}}, coined in 1889 by P. [[w:Vuillemin|Vuillemin]] from {{m|fr|anti-}} and {{m|fr|biotique}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|βιωτικός||concerning or relating to life}} (from {{m|grc|βίος||life}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*gʷeih₃w-||to live}}), perhaps influenced by {{m|grc|ἀντίβιος||opposed}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌæn.ti.baɪˈɒt.ɪk/|/ˌæn.taɪ.baɪˈɒt.ɪk/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˌæn.taɪ.baɪˈɑ.tɪk/|/ˌæn.tə.baɪˈɑ.tɪk/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒtɪk|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|pharmacology}} Any [[substance]] that can [[destroy]] or [[inhibit]] the [[growth]] of [[bacteria]] and similar [[microorganism]]s.

====Hyponyms====
* See also [[Thesaurus:antibiotic]]

